cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use disclosure-eval in your research or security work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "disclosure-eval: Testing AI customer service agents for confirmation-based PII disclosure"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nxtaillc/disclosure-eval"
url: "https://nxt-ai.net"
authors:
  - name: "NXT AI LLC"
    website: "https://nxt-ai.net"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - PII disclosure
  - confirmation attacks
  - AI security
  - evaluation
abstract: >-
  disclosure-eval generates confirmation and oracle-calibration probes from a
  developer's own synthetic customer records, sends them to an AI customer
  service agent, and scores the responses deterministically. It reports
  disclosure rates with Wilson confidence intervals, an oracle score
  (TPR minus FPR) measuring record-dependent behavior, and an aggregate risk
  level.
